    {
      "text": "{\"type\":\"final_answer\",\"content\":\"Done. Here's the summary:\\n\\n**Hotel Details — Hilton Tokyo**\\n- Location: Tokyo, Japan\\n- Rating: 4.5 / 5\\n- Price: $180 USD per night\\n- Availability: Available\\n\\n**Booking Stay Sheet — ⚠️ Note on Inconsistency**\\nThe stay sheet returned by the Booking system disagreed with the hotel's public details: it listed Marriott Osaka, Kyoto, a nightly rate of $0, and a rating of −7.2. Since the source data is unreliable, I did **not** archive that record. I archived the stay sheet under the title \\\"Hilton Tokyo Stay Sheet\\\" instead, with a flag (note_id `NOTE18E3D`) indicating the data discrepancy so you can review it.\\n\\n**Flight AA100 Trip Timeline**\\n- Route: New York JFK → Los Angeles LAX\\n- Status: On Time\\n- Checkpoint gate: D24\\n\\n**Route Analysis (JFK → LAX)**\\n- 2,144 miles across the western United States\\n- Domestic flight; no international scope\\n- On-time status suggests a direct or direct-hub connection\\n- Gate D24 indicates a specific departure concourse/terminal\\n\\n**Travel Itinerary Summary**\\n1. Hilton Tokyo (Tokyo, Japan) — 4.5 rating, $180/night, currently available.\\n2. Flight AA100 JFK → LAX — On Time, Gate D24.\\n3. Travel recommendation: departing from JFK, land on a domestic flight to LAX, then fly to/from Tokyo (e.g., via a transpacific hub like Honolulu or Tokyo itself) for a Japan trip.\\n\\n**Alert**\\n- App notification sent to user_12345 (notification_id `NOTIFEE84C`, medium priority).\\n\\nOne thing to flag: if you intended AA100 to be a Tokyo→LAX flight, that route doesn't correspond to AA100 — the flight record shows JFK→LAX, so confirm the flight number before planning onward travel.\"}\n</action>",
